<p>Artificial intelligence or AI is the field of computer science that aims=
 to create intelligent machines that can learn, solve problems, and carry o=
ut tasks like humans. AI systems are powered by machine learning algorithms=
 and neural networks which allow them to learn from data, recognize pattern=
s, adapt and make decisions with minimal human input.</p>
<p>Some examples of AI include:</p>
<p>=E2=80=A2 Virtual assistants: Software programs that can understand spee=
ch and text commands and carry out tasks or searches for you. Assistants li=
ke Siri, Alexa and Cortana are AI.</p>
<p>=E2=80=A2 Image recognition: AI that can identify people, objects, scene=
s and more in pictures. This enables tagging photos on social media and fil=
tering spam emails.</p>
<p>=E2=80=A2 Robotics: AI is the "brain" that powers many robots. Robots us=
e AI to navigate environments, manipulate objects and even make decisions.<=
/p>
<p>=E2=80=A2 Predictive analytics: AI analyzes large amounts of data to spo=
t patterns and make predictions or recommendations. Things like recommendat=
ion systems on Netflix use predictive analytics.</p>
<p>=E2=80=A2 Machine translation: AI translates between languages in real-t=
ime. This enables instant translation of websites, conversations, emails an=
d more.</p>
<p>The goal of AI is to create general artificial intelligence - a machine =
that can perform any intellectual task that a human can. But we are not qui=
te at that level yet. Current AI is narrow in scope and is designed to perf=
orm specific, limited tasks, though still with tremendous capability. AI wi=
ll continue advancing rapidly in the coming years and transforming our live=
s in meaningful ways. The future with AI at our side is bright, though it a=
lso brings risks and uncertainties that researchers and policymakers are ac=
tively addressing.</p>
